name    fuddleboard
prog    fuddle
# fuddle's board at a vt100.  It was built for a TeleVideo terminal --
# ESC = row col to place the cursor, ^Z to clear, ESC G4 for the reverse
# video its black pieces are drawn in -- and at an ANSI terminal the board
# never assembled.  tools/patch_fuddle.py (2026-09-26) gives each code its
# ANSI equivalent; the board then draws square by square, takes e2e4, and
# answers while `fuddling...' counts its search.
rate    0.3
wait    5
key     y
key     \r
wait    5
snap    board
keys    e2e4
key     \r
wait    25
snap    reply
key     \003
wait    3
expect   8  |  R  |||N|||  B  |||Q|||  K  |||B|||  N  |||R|||
expect   1  |||R|||  N  |||B|||  Q  |||K|||  B  |||N|||  R  |
expect  fuddling...
